WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:13.394
OPENED FROM ITS LINK
The site opened the model file from its link. Edits stay in this browser; Save or Export keeps them.

2
00:00:13.394 --> 00:00:24.169
PROPOSE A CHANGE
Propose a change leads to the repository's guide: changes come back through GitHub, by a branch or a fork and a pull request.

3
00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:32.383
HIDE THE MESSAGE
× hides the strip. Reloading the page fetches the model afresh and drops unsaved edits.

4
00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:43.425
THE EXPLORER
Kinds and Common hold what every layer shares. OA, SA, LA, PA and EPBS are the layers, from operations down to the product breakdown.

5
00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:52.111
THE VIEW TABS
Each tab shows the same model another way: diagrams, then tables, then analyses. General is open.

6
00:00:52.111 --> 00:01:01.117
FOLD THE BOTTOM PANEL
Problems, Text and more share the bottom panel. ▾ folds it down to its tabs, for more diagram.

7
00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:13.767
GENERAL VIEW: THE WHOLE MODEL
Unscoped, General draws all 853 boxes, the layers side by side from OA on the left to EPBS. ⤢ Fit shrinks them to specks, too small to read.

8
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:25.509
ZOOM IN AND SELECT
Wheel-zoom until the boxes read, then select one: the path above the canvas says where it lives. This one, taskSurveillanceArea, is in SA.

9
00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:36.655
SHOW ONE LAYER AT A TIME
So read one layer at a time: ⊞ beside a package shows only it in the diagrams. The chip above the canvas names it, here OA.

10
00:01:36.655 --> 00:01:46.987
OA ON ITS OWN
OA alone is 138 boxes. Select one and ◎ Selection zooms to it: SwarmMember, the drone. Properties shows its documentation.

11
00:01:46.987 --> 00:01:59.186
MOVE A BOX
Drag a box and it stays where you drop it, through edits and view switches; its lines follow. Dropping it onto another box would move it inside that box.

12
00:01:59.186 --> 00:02:09.653
AUTO-LAYOUT
Auto-layout forgets the boxes moved by hand and lays the view out afresh: SwarmMember is back where it was, beside watchAsset.

13
00:02:09.653 --> 00:02:18.434
BACK TO THE WHOLE MODEL
× on the chip shows the whole model again. Laying out all 853 boxes takes a few seconds.

14
00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:28.379
OPEN ANALYSIS
Analysis turns all 1373 elements into one network and ranks them. On the whole model that takes a couple of seconds.

15
00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:40.857
ANALYSIS
What holds the model together? Dots are elements, sized by their links; labels are thinned so none overlap. Hubs keep theirs: SwarmMember, TimeStamp, MemberId.

16
00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:52.079
REQUIREMENTS TABLE
What must hold, and what satisfies it? 49 requirements with their text and Satisfied By. Verified By is still empty in this model.

17
00:02:52.079 --> 00:03:03.024
ALLOCATION MATRIX
Which part performs which function? 106 functions against 23 parts, a tick per allocation: issueTasking goes to dutyController.

18
00:03:03.024 --> 00:03:15.013
SEQUENCE
Who sends what to whom, in order? Each flow is an arrow between lifelines. The first, handOverSectorAtoB: memberA proposes a sector handover to memberB.

19
00:03:15.013 --> 00:03:24.688
GRID
What is each element, and of what type? One row per element: here DetectionReport and its attributes, each with its type.

20
00:03:24.688 --> 00:03:36.025
CONTRACTS
What does each requirement assume and guarantee? DroneAirframeContract assumes a full charge at the start; it guarantees endurance and speed.

21
00:03:36.025 --> 00:03:47.763
THE MODEL AS TEXT
The Text tab holds the whole model as SysML-like text, kept in sync: a change made in a diagram shows up here. Export → SysML downloads it.
